#/Users/w.worawan/Downloads/ai-operation-microservice3_v2ori/requirements-pdf.in
#
# Source file for the version ranges the PDF admin review service (app_pdf.py)
# accepts — split off from requirements.in (2026-09) when the PDF review
# dashboard became its own deployable service, separate from the bot's
# requirements.txt. Deliberately lean: this service serves only
# router/admin_pdf.py's endpoints (pdf-queue list/detail/decision/reprocess),
# NOT the actual PDF extraction/OCR pipeline (service/pdf_large_extraction.py,
# service/pdf_dual_extraction.py) — that runs in service/sqs_consumer.py as
# its own separate, already-independent process (confirmed out of scope for
# this split) and needs its own heavier deps (pdf2image, pymupdf,
# typhoon_ocr) that this service never imports.
#
# Docker installs from the generated, exact-pinned + hash-locked
# requirements-pdf.txt, same pattern as requirements.in/.txt. Edit ranges
# here, then regenerate:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements-pdf.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.11 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu -o requirements-pdf.txt

